        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a765ba89-70db-5d18-9a5f-dc79540c5366",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mike Smith\n- Bands: Supergrass, Quietdrive, PJ Harvey, Elastica, Teenage Fan Club, Doves, Starsailor, The Beta Band, The Avalanches, Gorillaz, The White Stripes, The Libertines, Scissor Sisters, Arcade Fire, Arctic Monkeys, Blur\n- Companies: EMI Publishing\n- Places: Oxford, Hopkins, Minnesota\n- Topics: band formation, A&R signings\n\nFacts:\n- In 1992, Mike Smith moved to EMI Publishing.\n- At EMI Publishing, Mike Smith signed acts including PJ Harvey, Elastica, Supergrass, Teenage Fan Club, Doves, Starsailor, The Beta Band, The Avalanches, Gorillaz, The White Stripes, The Libertines, Scissor Sisters, Arcade Fire, and Arctic Monkeys.\n- At EMI Publishing, Mike Smith re-signed Blur and progressed to the position of Head of A&R.\n- In 1993, Supergrass formed in Oxford as an English rock band.\n- In 2002, Quietdrive formed as an alternative rock band based in Hopkins, Minnesota.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "bcb57594-5502-51ff-92ec-31ea6122000b",
        "text": "Page: Supergrass. Sentence: Supergrass were an English rock band, formed in 1993 in Oxford.\nPage: Quietdrive. Sentence: Quietdrive is an alternative rock band based in Hopkins, Minnesota that formed in 2002.\nPage: Mike Smith (A&amp;R man). Sentence: He then moved to EMI Publishing in 1992, where he went on to sign acts, such as PJ Harvey, Elastica, Supergrass, Teenage Fan Club, Doves, Starsailor, The Beta Band, The Avalanches, Gorillaz, The White Stripes, The Libertines, The Scissor Sisters, The Arcade Fire, and Arctic Monkeys, as well as resigning Blur and progressing to the position of Head of A&R.",
